From bdfa15b644bc27b4c5944be36003c0edc9ef41d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arlo O'Keeffe <tiger@k5d.de>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 13:47:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] support the "$/" self-repository `uses:` syntax

A `uses:` value starting with `$/` resolves against the repository running the
workflow at the exact commit running it, so it carries no `@ref` and needs no
checkout. GitHub added the form on 2026-07-30, and it is accepted everywhere the
workspace-relative `./` form is: workflow steps, composite action steps, nested
composition, and reusable workflow calls.

Both forms name the same file, so `canonLocalUsesSpec` normalises `$/{path}` to
`./{path}` rather than teaching every call site a second prefix. The metadata
caches are keyed by spec: a reusable workflow reached as `./x.yml` from one
caller and `$/x.yml` from another has to hit the same entry, and
`LocalReusableWorkflowCache.WriteWorkflowCallEvent` writes its keys in the `./`
form.

`isWorkflowCallUsesRepoFormat` needed the prefix as well. It rejects a leading
`.` so a local call is never mistaken for a repository one; without the same
guard, `$/path/to/x.yml@ref` parsed as owner `$`, repo `path` and was accepted
as a valid repository reference rather than reported.

Closes #711

